.TH SHUTDOWN 2
.SH NAME
shutdown \- disable one direction of a local socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.PP
.B int shutdown(int socket, int how);
.SH DESCRIPTION
shutdown() disables reception for SHUT_RD, transmission for SHUT_WR, or
both directions for SHUT_RDWR. Astia implements this operation for connected
AF_UNIX SOCK_STREAM socketpairs.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success, or -1 and sets errno on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EBADF
socket is not an open descriptor.
.TP
.B EINVAL
how is not SHUT_RD, SHUT_WR, or SHUT_RDWR, or socket is not connected.
